hgzSay("Melanthius, the goatherd", "Melanthius, with the best goats for the suitors", "😠 You again", ["\"Here vagrant, still? offensive to my lords!\nBlows have more energy than airy words;"], hgBk(20)),
hgzId("cow", hgzRead("🐄 Philoetius", hgQs("From Cephanelia 'cross the surgy main\nPhilaetius late arrived, a faithful swain.") + "<p>The cowherd, who has kept his master's cattle on the mainland for twenty years, comes in with a heifer for the feast, and looks hard at the beggar.</p>" + hgSrc(hgBk(20)), "▶ Go on")),
hgzSay("Philoetius, the cowherd", "Philoetius, taking the beggar's hand", "🤝 You remind me of him", ["\"Stranger, may fate a milder aspect show,\nAnd spin thy future with a whiter clue!"], hgBk(20)),
hgzPuzzle("🕊️ The omen", "The suitors, out in the fields, are plotting to kill Telemachus. Then a bird flies over on their left. What is it?", ["A swan flying south", "An eagle with a trembling dove in its claws", "A flock of crows"], 1, ["No.", "", "No."], { yes: "🕊️ " + hgQ("When in his airy tour, the bird of Jove\nTruss'd with his sinewy pounce a trembling dove;\nSinister to their hope!") + " Amphinomus tells them to give it up and go and eat." }),
hgzId("feast", hgzGo(hgR("megaron", 0, 4), "Into the hall: the suitors are at the feast. Telemachus has put the beggar at a little table by the threshold", { r: 3 })),
hgzRead("🦶 A cow's hoof", "<p>Ctesippus, a rich suitor from Same, says the guest should have a gift too, and hurls an ox-hoof at him from the basket.</p>" + hgQs("Which whizzing high, the wall unseemly sign'd.\nThe chief indignant grins a ghastly smile;") + hgSrc(hgBk(20)), "▶ Go on"),
hgzRead("😱 Laughter", hgQs("But Pallas clouds with intellectual gloom\nThe suitors' souls, insensate of their doom!\nA mirthful frenzy seized the fated crowd;\nThe roofs resound with causeless laughter loud;") + hgSrc(hgBk(20)), "▶ Go on"),
hgzSay("Theoclymenus, the seer", "Theoclymenus, on his feet", "👁️ I see", ["\"O race to death devote! with Stygian shade\nEach destin'd peer impending fates invade;", "Thick swarms the spacious hall with howling ghosts,"], hgBk(20)),
hgzId("seergone", hgzRead("🚪 He goes", hgQs("This said, to sage Piraeus sped the seer,\nHis honour'd host, a welcome inmate there.") + "<p>They laugh him out of the house. Telemachus says nothing. He only watches his father, waiting for the sign.</p>" + hgSrc(hgBk(20)), "▶ To Book XXI"))
