hgzSay("Priam, king of Troy", "Priam, tearing his white hair", "😭 Come inside", ["\"Ah stay not, stay not! guardless and alone;\nHector! my loved, my dearest, bravest son!", "Yet shun Achilles! enter yet the wall;\nAnd spare thyself, thy father, spare us all!"], hgBk(22)),
hgzSay("Hecuba, queen of Troy", "Hecuba, his mother", "😭 I nursed you", ["\"Have mercy on me, O my son! revere\nThe words of age; attend a parent's prayer!"], hgBk(22)),
hgzRead("🐍 Like a snake", "<p>He will not come in. He waits for Achilles like a mountain snake at its hole. He thinks: Polydamas told me to bring the army in last night, and I would not listen, and now so many are dead because of me. If I go in, they will say: Hector trusted his own strength and destroyed his people. Better to meet Achilles. Could I put down my shield, and go to him, and promise to give back Helen and all the treasure, and half of everything in Troy? No: he would kill me like a woman, unarmed.</p>" + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), "▶ Go on"),
hgzId("chase", hgzRead("🏃 He runs", hgQs("As Hector sees, unusual terrors rise,\nStruck by some god, he fears, recedes, and flies.\nHe leaves the gates, he leaves the wall behind:\nAchilles follows like the winged wind.") + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), "▶ Go on")),
hgzGo("trFig", "Down off the wall and after them: past the lookout, along the wagon-road under the wall to the wild fig tree", { r: 8 }),
hgzGo("trSprings", "On to the two springs where the Scamander rises, one hot and one cold", { r: 8 }),
hgzRead("💧 The two springs", hgQs("Next by Scamander's double source they bound,\nWhere two famed fountains burst the parted ground;\nThis hot through scorching clefts is seen to rise,\nWith exhalations steaming to the skies;\nThat the green banks in summer's heat o'erflows,\nLike crystal clear, and cold as winter snows:", "Where Trojan dames (ere yet alarm'd by Greece)\nWash'd their fair garments in the days of peace.") + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), "▶ Go on"),
hgzGo(hgA("trGate", -12, 0), "Round, and back to the Scaean Gate", { r: 6 }),
hgzPuzzle("🔁 How many times?", "How many times do they run round the walls of Troy?", ["Once", "Three times", "Seven times"], 1, ["", "", ""], { yes: "🔁 " + hgQ("Thus three times round the Trojan wall they fly.\nThe gazing gods lean forward from the sky;") }),
hgzRead("⚖️ The scales", hgQs("Jove lifts the golden balances, that show\nThe fates of mortal men, and things below:\nHere each contending hero's lot he tries,\nAnd weighs, with equal hand, their destinies.\nLow sinks the scale surcharged with Hector's fate;") + "<p>And Apollo leaves him.</p>" + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), "▶ Go on"),
hgzId("stand", hgzSay("Deiphobus (Athena)", "Athena, in the shape of his brother Deiphobus", "🤝 I'm with you", ["\"Too long, O Hector! have I borne the sight\nOf this distress, and sorrow'd in thy flight:\nIt fits us now a noble stand to make,\nAnd here, as brothers, equal fates partake.\""], hgBk(22))),
hgzSay("Hector", "Hector, to Achilles", "🤝 Swear an oath", ["\"Enough, O son of Peleus! Troy has view'd\nHer walls thrice circled, and her chief pursued.\nBut now some god within me bids me try\nThine, or my fate: I kill thee, or I die."], hgBk(22)),
hgzSay("Achilles", "Achilles", "😡 No oaths", ["\"Talk not of oaths (the dreadful chief replies,\nWhile anger flash'd from his disdainful eyes),", "Such pacts as lambs and rabid wolves combine,\nSuch leagues as men and furious lions join,"], hgBk(22)),
hgzId("spear", hgzRead("🗡️ No brother", "<p>Achilles' spear misses, and Athena gives it back to him without Hector seeing. Hector's spear strikes the middle of the god-made shield and bounces off. He shouts to Deiphobus for another spear: and there is no one there. Then he knows.</p>" + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), "▶ Go on")),
hgzId("dead", hgzReadA("💔 Hector", hgQs("Fierce, at the word, his weighty sword he drew,\nAnd, all collected, on Achilles flew.") + "<p>Achilles knows every weak place in his own old armour, which Hector is wearing; and he finds the one place where the neck is open, by the collarbone.</p>" + hgQs("Then Hector, fainting at the approach of death:\n\"By thy own soul! by those who gave thee breath!\nBy all the sacred prevalence of prayer;\nAh, leave me not for Grecian dogs to tear!") + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), hgQs("Fierce, at the word, his weighty sword he drew,\nAnd, all collected, on Achilles flew.") + "<p>But Achilles knows his own old armour, which Hector is wearing; and Hector falls. Dying, he begs Achilles to give his body back to his father and mother.</p>" + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), "▶ Go on")),
hgzSay("Hector", "Hector, dying", "⚰️ Remember", ["\"Thy rage, implacable! too well I knew:", "Phoebus and Paris shall avenge my fate,\nAnd stretch thee here before the Scaean gate.\""], hgBk(22)),
hgzId("ghost", hgzRead("👻 A naked ghost", hgQs("He ceased. The Fates suppress'd his labouring breath,\nAnd his eyes stiffen'd at the hand of death;\nTo the dark realm the spirit wings its way,") + "<p>Then Achilles does a shameful thing. He ties Hector's body by the ankles to his chariot, and drags it in the dust toward the ships, in front of the walls, in front of his father and mother.</p>" + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), "▶ Go on")),
hgzFind("hectorplume", hgA("trGate", -20, 4), "A black horsehair from Hector's crest", "In the dust by the gate lies a long black horsehair from his helmet. Pick it up, for those who loved him", { r: 2 }),
hgzId("loom", hgzGo(hgR("hector", 0, 2.2), "Through the gate and the town to Hector's house. Andromache has not heard: she is at her loom", { r: 2.4 })),
hgzRead("🧵 The loom", hgQs("Far in the close recesses of the dome,\nPensive she plied the melancholy loom;\nA growing work employ'd her secret hours,\nConfusedly gay with intermingled flowers.\nHer fair-haired handmaids heat the brazen urn,\nThe bath preparing for her lord's return") + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), "▶ Go on"),
hgzId("wall", hgzGo(hgA("trTower", -1, 0), "She hears the wailing from the walls, and the shuttle falls from her hand. She runs, and you run with her, to the tower", { r: 4 })),
hgzSay("Andromache", "Andromache, on the wall", "😭 Wretched wife", ["\"O wretched husband of a wretched wife!\nBorn with one fate, to one unhappy life!", "To my sad soul Astyanax appears!"], hgBk(22)),
hgzRead("🌑 She falls", "<p>She sees him dragged across the plain, and black night comes over her eyes, and she falls back, and the bright ribbons fly from her hair: the veil that Aphrodite gave her on her wedding day, when Hector came for her from her father's house.</p>" + hgSrc(hgBk(22)), "▶ To Book XXIII")
